1
00:00:00,870 --> 00:00:01,500
I love parades.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:06,490
The Thanksgiving Day parade is always such great fun.

3
00:00:06,490 --> 00:00:09,740
Look at that Superman balloon!

4
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:16,190
Wowee! Just floating along high above Central Park West.

5
00:00:16,190 --> 00:00:18,490
Don't you just love it?

6
00:00:18,490 --> 00:00:21,320
Oh, and the bands and the music.

7
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:22,600
John Philip Sousa.

8
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,340
I love his music.

9
00:00:24,340 --> 00:00:31,620
Da dada da da dada da da da da da da dada.

10
00:00:31,620 --> 00:00:35,730
Oh, look at that float, Robbie.

11
00:00:35,730 --> 00:00:38,160
Look at those funny-looking clowns.

12
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:40,480
It's for kids.

13
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:44,450
Maybe so, but parades always make me feel like a kid.

14
00:00:44,450 --> 00:00:47,760
Remember when you and your dad and I

15
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:51,600
went to the Thanksgiving Day parade?

16
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:59,480
You were four or five years old, I think.

17
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:03,250
Hello, hello.... Oh, hi, Susan.

18
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:09,280
How are you?... Here's Mom.

19
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:11,330
Hello, Susan.

20
00:01:11,330 --> 00:01:15,050
Yes, he missed a phone call from Alexandra.

21
00:01:15,050 --> 00:01:17,530
Yes, I know, but he'll get over it.

22
00:01:17,530 --> 00:01:20,300
Good. Then you'll be here about five?

23
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:21,720
Oh, fine.

24
00:01:21,720 --> 00:01:25,700
I look forward to seeing you and Harry and Michelle.

25
00:01:25,700 --> 00:01:27,390
Drive carefully.

26
00:01:27,390 --> 00:01:29,540
Good-bye.

27
00:01:29,540 --> 00:01:30,640
Taste Ellen's turkey dressing.

28
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:33,160
It's delicious.

29
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,450
I'm not surprised.

30
00:01:34,450 --> 00:01:36,090
It's Grandma's recipe.

31
00:01:36,090 --> 00:01:37,810
It's my favorite part of the meal.

32
00:01:37,810 --> 00:01:40,280
What about my famous apple pie?

33
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:44,380
Dad, your apple pie is my favorite dessert.

34
00:01:44,380 --> 00:01:45,520
How's the parade?

35
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:56,490
OK.

36
00:01:56,490 --> 00:01:58,840
Mom! Is it for me?

37
00:01:58,840 --> 00:02:00,260
No, Robbie.

38
00:02:00,260 --> 00:02:02,530
Who was it?

39
00:02:02,530 --> 00:02:04,180
Wrong number.

40
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:06,420
Philip, would you join me in the kitchen, please?

41
00:02:06,420 --> 00:02:07,120
It's getting late.

42
00:02:07,120 --> 00:02:08,940
We have vegetables to prepare.

43
00:02:08,940 --> 00:02:09,900
Can I help with anything?

44
00:02:09,900 --> 00:02:10,470
No, honey.

45
00:02:10,470 --> 00:02:11,870
You just relax with Grandpa.

46
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:15,490
I'll get you to help serve later.

47
00:02:15,490 --> 00:02:18,360
Ellen reminds me so much of Grandma.

48
00:02:18,360 --> 00:02:20,380
What time does the Michigan football game come on?

49
00:02:20,380 --> 00:02:21,060
Four.

50
00:02:21,060 --> 00:02:23,000
Philip!

51
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,870
I'll be back to see the game.

52
00:02:26,870 --> 00:02:30,920
Grandpa, when did Dad graduate from Michigan?

53
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:32,690
Let me think.

54
00:02:32,690 --> 00:02:36,340
He graduated from medical school in 1960

55
00:02:36,340 --> 00:02:41,160
and from the University of Michigan in 1956.

56
00:02:41,160 --> 00:02:42,530
Did you go to Michigan, too, Grandpa?

57
00:02:42,530 --> 00:02:46,920
Yup. I graduated in 1937.

58
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:49,920
I've got to start thinking about college soon.
